    <h1>BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding</h1>
    <p>BERT, which stands for Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers, is a landmark model in Natural Language Processing (NLP). Developed by Google Research in 2018, it changed how machines understand human language.</p>
    
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>Unlike previous models that read text from left-to-right (or right-to-left), BERT reads the entire sequence of words at once. This allows it to learn the context of a word based on all of its surroundings (both to the left and the right of the word).</p>
    
    <h2>Key Innovations</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Masked Language Model (MLM):</strong> Randomly masking some of the tokens from the input, and the objective is to predict the original vocabulary id of the masked word based only on its context.</li>
        <li><strong>Next Sentence Prediction (NSP):</strong> Training the model to understand the relationship between two sentences.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>For more search results, try searching for "Transformers" or "Language Models" in the agent!</p>
